== Sunday School

There's a kid in Sunday School
  who always asks questions

What about this? How did that happen?

The tone of the lesson changes
Short answers; back on topic
Like a drive on the the camp road
Dodging poholes and squirrels

The impatiences tastes like mediocre coffee
Stale cookies; smells like floral perfume

The questions don't go away, they're just asked to
Other people

There's a kid in Sunday School
  who stopped asking questions
  who looks at St. Thomas
  understands him

There's a kid in Sunday School
  who is not doubting Thomas
  but a curious Thomas
  who didn't have a
  patient Jesus to ask

Where is that kid now?
